[
  {
    "text": "Trait boredom, as a stable individual difference, may be elevated in adults with ADHD symptoms even if state boredom fluctuates differently, so claims about one do not automatically generalize to the other.",
    "topic": "Distinction between trait and state boredom"
  },
  {
    "text": "Attention control deficits could partially mediate the relationship between ADHD symptoms and trait boredom, meaning the observed higher trait boredom might be both directly and indirectly linked to ADHD symptoms.",
    "topic": "Mediation role of attention control"
  },
  {
    "text": "Resolving the contradiction requires testing a mediation model in a single sample that simultaneously estimates direct and indirect effects of ADHD symptoms on boredom through attention control.",
    "topic": "Mediation analysis specification"
  },
  {
    "text": "Differences in the severity of ADHD symptoms (e.g., subthreshold vs. diagnosed) across studies could explain contradictions, so replicating the finding with a stratified sample by symptom severity could clarify.",
    "topic": "Severity stratification"
  }
]
